    "## Contextual BM25\n",
    "\n",
    "Contextual embeddings is an improvement on traditional semantic search RAG, but we can improve performance further. In this section we'll show you how you can use contextual embeddings and *contextual* BM25 together. enquanto you can see performance gains by pairing these techniques together without the context, adding context to these Métodos reduces the top-20-chunk retrieval failure rate by 42%.\n",
    "\n",
    "BM25 is a probabilistic ranking função that improves upon TF-IDF. isso scores documents based on query term frequency, enquanto accounting para document length and term saturation. BM25 is widely used in modern search motores para its effectiveness in ranking relevant documents. para more details, see [this blog post](https://www.elastic.co/blog/practical-bm25-part-2-the-bm25-algorithm-and-its-variables). We'll use elastic search para the BM25 portion of this section, which will require you to have the elasticsearch library installed and isso will also require you to spin up an Elasticsearch server in the background. The easiest way to do this is to install [docker](https://docs.docker.com/engine/install/) and run the following docker command:\n",
    "\n",
    "`docker run -d --nome elasticsearch -p 9200:9200 -p 9300:9300 -e \"discovery.tipo=single-node\" -e \"xpack.security.enabled=falso\" elasticsearch:8.8.0`\n",
    "\n",
    "One difference between a typical BM25 search and what we'll do in this section is that, para each chunk, we'll run each BM25 search on both the chunk content and the additional context that we generated in the previous section. From there, we'll use a technique called reciprocal rank fusion to merge the results from our BM25 search with our semantic search results. This allows us to perform a hybrid search across both our BM25 corpus and vector DB to retornar the most optimal documents para a given query.\n",
    "\n",
    "In the função below, we allow you the option to add weightings to the semantic search and BM25 search documents as you merge them with Reciprocal Rank Fusion. By padrão, we definir these to 0.8 para the semantic search results and 0.2 to the BM25 results. We'd encourage you to experiment with different values here."
   ]
